# Flow Vello Project Rules

- Treat `AGENTS.md` as the primary project contract.
- Preserve the established Flow Vello visual system; do not introduce a disconnected UI style.
- Build static-first HTML pages with reusable CSS/JS patterns.
- Keep navigation, footer, buttons, typography, spacing, animation, and responsive behavior consistent.
- Use semantic HTML, accessible controls, one H1 per page, descriptive alt text, and keyboard support.
- Every public page needs unique title, description, canonical, Open Graph metadata, and appropriate JSON-LD.
- Never fabricate social proof, client work, statistics, testimonials, certifications, or business details.
- Prefer existing dependencies and patterns before adding a new dependency.
- Do not expose secrets or hard-code credentials.
- Before finishing, inspect the affected page at desktop/mobile widths, verify links/assets, and check for console errors.
